<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <a href="/docs/scripting" class="inline-flex items-center text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300 font-medium transition-colors group">
      <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2 transform group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path></svg>
      Lua Scripting Overview
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="relative">
      <div class="absolute -inset-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-indigo-600 rounded-lg blur opacity-25"></div>
      <div class="relative">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-400 via-indigo-400 to-purple-400 mb-4 tracking-tight">Validation</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
          Validate and sanitize user input with built-in helpers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Validation -->
    <section id="validation">
      <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center mt-0 border-0">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-pink-500 mr-2"></span>
            Validation
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8">
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-4">Validate data against a <strong class="text-gray-300">JSON Schema</strong> written as a Lua table. The full draft 2020-12 vocabulary is supported: <code>type</code>, <code>properties</code>, <code>required</code>, <code>minimum</code>/<code>maximum</code>, <code>minLength</code>/<code>maxLength</code>, <code>pattern</code>, <code>format</code>, <code>enum</code>, <code>items</code>, and so on.</p>
           <ul class="space-y-3 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-3 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-purple-400">solidb.validate(data, schema)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; bool</span>
               <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">
                 Returns <code>true</code> if <code>data</code> conforms to the schema, <code>false</code> otherwise. Raises an error if the schema itself is invalid.
               </div>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-3 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-purple-400">solidb.validate_detailed(data, schema)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table</span>
               <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">
                 Returns <code>{ valid = true, errors = {} }</code>, or <code>{ valid = false, error_count = n, errors = { { message, path, schema_path }, ... } }</code> so the client can be told exactly which field failed.
               </div>
             </li>
           </ul>

           <div class="bg-gray-950 rounded-xl border border-white/10 overflow-hidden shadow-xl mt-6">
                <div class="p-4 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
<pre class="language-lua"><span class="text-blue-400">local</span> schema = {
  type = <span class="text-green-400">"object"</span>,
  required = { <span class="text-green-400">"name"</span> },
  properties = {
    name  = { type = <span class="text-green-400">"string"</span>, minLength = <span class="text-purple-400">3</span> },
    age   = { type = <span class="text-green-400">"integer"</span>, minimum = <span class="text-purple-400">18</span> },
    email = { type = <span class="text-green-400">"string"</span>, format = <span class="text-green-400">"email"</span> }
  }
}

<span class="text-gray-500">-- Quick check: reject with a 400</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">if</span> <span class="text-blue-400">not</span> <span class="text-pink-400">solidb.validate</span>(request.body, schema) <span class="text-blue-400">then</span>
  <span class="text-pink-400">solidb.error</span>(<span class="text-green-400">"Invalid payload"</span>, <span class="text-purple-400">400</span>)
<span class="text-blue-400">end</span>

<span class="text-gray-500">-- Or report every failing field</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">local</span> result = <span class="text-pink-400">solidb.validate_detailed</span>(request.body, schema)
<span class="text-blue-400">if</span> <span class="text-blue-400">not</span> result.valid <span class="text-blue-400">then</span>
  <span class="text-blue-400">return</span> response.json({ errors = result.errors }, <span class="text-purple-400">422</span>)
<span class="text-blue-400">end</span></pre>
                </div>
           </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Sanitization -->
    <section id="sanitization">
      <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center mt-0 border-0">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-teal-500 mr-2"></span>
            Sanitization
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8">
           <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-4">Normalise a string or a whole table in one call by listing the operations to apply.</p>
           <ul class="space-y-3 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-3 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-purple-400">solidb.sanitize(data, operations)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; value</span>
               <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">
                 Returns a cleaned copy of <code>data</code>. Each operation is either <code>true</code> (apply to every string field) or an array of field names to restrict it to.<br><br>
                 <strong class="text-gray-400">Operations:</strong>
                 <ul class="mt-1 ml-4 space-y-1">
                   <li><code>trim</code>: strip leading and trailing whitespace</li>
                   <li><code>lowercase</code>, <code>uppercase</code>: change case</li>
                   <li><code>normalize_whitespace</code>: collapse runs of whitespace to a single space</li>
                   <li><code>strip_html</code>: remove HTML tags</li>
                   <li><code>lowercase_keys</code>, <code>trim_keys</code>: apply to the table's keys instead of its values</li>
                 </ul>
               </div>
             </li>
           </ul>

           <div class="bg-gray-950 rounded-xl border border-white/10 overflow-hidden shadow-xl mt-6">
                <div class="p-4 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
<pre class="language-lua"><span class="text-blue-400">local</span> clean = <span class="text-pink-400">solidb.sanitize</span>(request.body, {
  trim = <span class="text-blue-400">true</span>,
  strip_html = { <span class="text-green-400">"bio"</span>, <span class="text-green-400">"comment"</span> },
  lowercase = { <span class="text-green-400">"email"</span> }
})

db:collection(<span class="text-green-400">"profiles"</span>):insert(clean)</pre>
                </div>
           </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
